# Backend build context exclusions.
#
# Everything here is either a build artefact, a local secret, or a file that must
# never reach an image layer. The context is `backend/`, so the duplicate
# `padhaanewala/bot_robot.glb` at the repository root is outside it entirely and
# cannot be sent to the daemon by this build.

# --- Secrets. The single most important entry in this file. -------------
# `.env.development` holds real generated SECRET_KEY / JWT_SECRET_KEY values and
# is gitignored, but `.dockerignore` is what stops it being sent to the daemon and
# baked into a layer where `docker history` would reveal it. Both patterns are
# listed because a file called `.env.production` is exactly what someone creates
# when they go to deploy.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
secrets/
*.pem
*.key

# --- Captured process output -------------------------------------------
# A SQLAlchemy error message embeds the connection string, credentials
# included. `.gitignore` gained `*.err` and `*.out` in Phase 1.10 for exactly
# this reason; `*.log` does not match a uvicorn stderr capture. This directory
# currently holds `uvi.err` and `uvi.log` from a previous local run, and they
# must not be copied into a published image.
*.log
*.err
*.out

# --- Virtualenv. Created inside backend/ by the documented setup step. ---
# 49 packages, ~400 MB, rebuilt identically in the image. Copying it in would
# also bake a Windows-path interpreter into a Linux image.
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Tests and tooling. Not needed at runtime. --------------------------
# `test_session_security.py` and friends are Phase 3 regression coverage that
# belongs in CI, not in a production image where it cannot be executed anyway
# (no pytest, no test schema).
tests/
pytest.ini
.coverage
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

# --- scripts/ is NOT excluded. ------------------------------------------
# A fresh database needs `seed_roles.py` before *any* registration can succeed
# (register is fail-closed on a missing student role and returns 503), and
# Phase 8.3 bootstraps the first admin with `seed_admin.py`. Keeping them out of
# the image would mean the only way to seed is a host checkout, which is one more
# thing to get wrong on a first deploy.
#
# `purge_demo_data.py` is the exception: it deletes rows, and a data-destroying
# script has no business being present in a production image where a mistyped
# command is unrecoverable.
scripts/purge_demo_data.py

# bootstrap_test_db.py points at PADHAANEWALA_SCHEMA and creates a scratch
# schema. Harmless, but it belongs to the test workflow, not to a deployed app.
scripts/bootstrap_test_db.py

# --- Migrations ARE required at runtime (alembic upgrade head runs on
# deploy), so alembic/ and alembic.ini are deliberately NOT excluded.

# --- Caches / editors / OS ---------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
